WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Imagine waking up ten years from now.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.248
You don’t open dozens of apps to get
things done.

00:00:07.248 --> 00:00:11.256
Instead, you simply tell your AI what you
want.

00:00:11.256 --> 00:00:13.056
“Plan my day.”

00:00:13.056 --> 00:00:23.064
Your AI checks your schedule, understands
your priorities, prepares your work,
responds to routine messages, and tells
you what actually needs your attention.

00:00:23.064 --> 00:00:27.264
But the biggest change isn’t that AI can
answer questions.

00:00:27.264 --> 00:00:30.624
It’s that AI can take action.

00:00:30.624 --> 00:00:35.088
Today, we use software by clicking buttons
and navigating menus.

00:00:35.088 --> 00:00:45.048
Tomorrow, we may interact with software
more like we interact with people: by
describing an outcome and letting
intelligent agents figure out the steps.

00:00:45.048 --> 00:00:54.768
Businesses could have AI agents managing
sales operations, analyzing finances,
supporting customers, writing software,
and coordinating entire workflows.

00:00:54.768 --> 00:01:02.832
And that creates a fascinating shift: the
most valuable skill may no longer be
knowing exactly how to do every task.

00:01:02.832 --> 00:01:09.552
It may be knowing what should be done, why
it matters, and how to direct intelligent
systems to accomplish it.

00:01:09.552 --> 00:01:13.008
AI isn't simply changing the tools we use.

00:01:13.008 --> 00:01:15.816
It may change what it means to use a
computer.
